Article 2 (Application for Authorization of Ship Investment Business)
(1) A person who intends to obtain authorization for ship investment business under Article 13 (1) of the Ship Investment Company Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") shall prepare and submit to the Minister of Oceans and Fisheries an application for authorization stating the following matters: <Amended on Dec. 28, 2005; Mar. 14, 2008; Mar. 24, 2013; Jan. 2, 2017>
1. Trade name;
2. Location of the principal office;
3. Names, dates of birth, and addresses of executives;
4. Matters concerning capital;
5. Names, gross tonnage, and other specifications of vessels owned.
(2) The following documents shall be attached to an application for authorization under paragraph (1):
1. Articles of incorporation;
2. Minutes of the inaugural general meeting;
3. Documents concerning the careers of executives;
4. Written evidence of payment for shares;
5. A document stating the status of subscriptions for shares by promoters as of the application date, the status of major shareholders, and the numbers of shares they hold;
6. Business plan;
7. Copies of contracts for entrustment of business with a ship management company and an asset custody company.
